<mjml lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-title>The Workbench — Issue 42: desk ergonomics that actually stick</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>Issue 42: the three ergonomics changes that survive a busy week.</mj-preview>

    <mj-raw>
      <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
      <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark">
    </mj-raw>

    <mj-font name="Inter" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;700" />

    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="Inter, Arial, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text color="#2b2b2b" font-size="15px" line-height="24px" padding="8px 24px" />
      <mj-divider border-color="#e3e6ea" border-width="1px" border-style="solid" padding="16px 24px" />
      <mj-class name="h1" font-size="26px" line-height="34px" font-weight="700" color="#121212" />
      <mj-class name="h2" font-size="19px" line-height="26px" font-weight="700" color="#121212" />
      <mj-class name="meta" font-size="12px" line-height="18px" color="#5a5a5a" />
    </mj-attributes>

    <mj-html-attributes>
      <mj-selector path=".email-heading div">
        <mj-html-attribute name="role">heading</mj-html-attribute>
        <mj-html-attribute name="aria-level">1</mj-html-attribute>
      </mj-selector>
      <mj-selector path=".story-heading div">
        <mj-html-attribute name="role">heading</mj-html-attribute>
        <mj-html-attribute name="aria-level">2</mj-html-attribute>
      </mj-selector>
    </mj-html-attributes>

    <!-- Light logo visible by default; dark logo hidden -->
    <mj-style inline="inline">
      .dark-logo { display: none !important; }
    </mj-style>

    <!-- Dark mode overrides -->
    <mj-style>
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .light-logo { display: none !important; }
        .dark-logo  { display: block !important; }
        .dm-bg      { background-color: #121212 !important; }
        .dm-card    { background-color: #1e1e1e !important; }
        .dm-text div { color: #F1F1F1 !important; }
        .dm-muted div { color: #b9b9b9 !important; }
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#f1f1f1" width="600px" css-class="dm-bg">

    <mj-wrapper background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 0" css-class="dm-card">

      <mj-section padding="0">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-image css-class="light-logo" src="https://cdn.example.com/workbench-logo-light.png" alt="The Workbench" width="180px" href="https://example.com" padding="0 24px 4px" />
          <mj-image css-class="dark-logo" src="https://cdn.example.com/workbench-logo-dark.png" alt="The Workbench" width="180px" href="https://example.com" padding="0 24px 4px" />
          <mj-text mj-class="meta" css-class="dm-muted" align="center">Issue 42 &middot; 10 August 2026</mj-text>
          <mj-divider />
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <mj-section padding="0">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text css-class="email-heading dm-text" mj-class="h1">
            Desk ergonomics that actually stick
          </mj-text>
          <mj-text css-class="dm-text">
            Most ergonomics advice fails because it asks you to remember something.
            The three changes below work because they are physical defaults — once set,
            they hold without any effort from you.
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <mj-section padding="0">
        <mj-column width="35%" vertical-align="top">
          <mj-image src="https://cdn.example.com/story-monitor.jpg" alt="A monitor raised to eye level on a wooden riser" width="170px" padding="8px 0 8px 24px" />
        </mj-column>
        <mj-column width="65%" vertical-align="top">
          <mj-text css-class="story-heading dm-text" mj-class="h2">1. Raise the monitor, not the chair</mj-text>
          <mj-text css-class="dm-text">
            The top of the screen should sit level with your eyes. Raising the chair
            instead just moves the problem to your feet.
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <mj-section padding="0">
        <mj-column width="35%" vertical-align="top">
          <mj-image src="https://cdn.example.com/story-keyboard.jpg" alt="A split keyboard positioned at elbow height" width="170px" padding="8px 0 8px 24px" />
        </mj-column>
        <mj-column width="65%" vertical-align="top">
          <mj-text css-class="story-heading dm-text" mj-class="h2">2. Set the keyboard to elbow height</mj-text>
          <mj-text css-class="dm-text">
            Forearms parallel to the floor. If the desk cannot go lower, a keyboard
            tray costs less than a new desk and fixes the same problem.
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <mj-section padding="0">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-divider />
          <mj-text mj-class="meta" css-class="dm-muted">
            You are receiving this because you subscribed at example.com.
            <a href="https://example.com/unsubscribe" style="color:#5a5a5a;">Unsubscribe</a>
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

    </mj-wrapper>

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
